Slide 2 – Project Overview

Time: 1 minute

Before going into the technical implementation, let us understand the problem we are trying to solve.

Stock prices are influenced by several factors, including company announcements, financial results, market trends, and external events.

However, financial news and stock market prices are generally available as separate data sources.

Our project brings these two sources together.

We collect financial news from Google News RSS and stock price information from a Market Data API.

The collected information is first ingested into Kafka, which acts as our distributed event streaming platform.

After ingestion, the data follows different processing paths. News data is stored in the Bronze layer before being processed in Silver, whereas stock data is consumed directly from Kafka by its Silver processing pipeline.

Once both streams are processed and standardized, they are brought together in the Gold layer.

The Gold layer performs time-based aggregation and connects news sentiment with stock price movements.

Finally, the processed information is intended to be presented through a Streamlit dashboard.

So, the main objective is not just collecting data, but building a pipeline that can process, validate, correlate, and serve financial data.

