Slide 8 – Phase 4: Gold Aggregation and Dashboard Serving

Time: 1 minute 45 seconds

Phase 4 focuses on combining the processed news and stock information in the Gold layer.

At this stage, we already have two structured Silver outputs.

The first input is "silver/news_by_ticker", which contains company-specific news records along with their sentiment scores.

The second input is "silver/stock", which contains validated stock price observations.

The Gold processing logic is implemented in "gold_job.py" using PySpark Structured Streaming.

The two streams are joined using the canonical ticker and event-time information.

This allows the pipeline to correlate news associated with a particular company with stock observations for that same company.

We use event-time processing because the actual time of an event is more meaningful for financial analysis than simply relying on the time at which our system received the event.

The aggregation uses a five-minute window with a one-minute sliding interval.

This means that the pipeline calculates metrics over five-minute periods and updates the overlapping windows at one-minute intervals.

We also configure a ten-minute watermark.

A watermark helps the streaming engine manage late-arriving events and determine how long it should wait for delayed records before finalizing window results.

The Gold aggregation calculates metrics such as average sentiment, stock price movement, and article count.

The output is stored in "gold/sentiment_price" using Delta Lake and PostgreSQL.

The dashboard is developed using Streamlit in "app.py".

The planned dashboard provides a company dropdown, a news-versus-stock-price movement chart, sentiment distribution, company-wise comparison, and key market metrics.

The purpose is to make the relationship between financial news and stock movement easier to explore.

The dashboard currently uses sample or prototype data. The live connection to the Gold and PostgreSQL outputs is still pending.

